  "notes": "The same entity as Home Assistant 2026.10.4 sends it with unit_system us_customary: weatherflow_cloud.json's values fed to Home Assistant's WeatherEntity as native values in the units its attributes state (°C, hPa, km/h, km, mm), state and forecasts read back through the weather component with hass.config.units set to US_CUSTOMARY_SYSTEM. Temperatures come back as whole °F (ints: outside °C the weather entity rounds to whole degrees), pressure in inHg, wind in mph, visibility in mi and precipitation in in, each to 2 decimals; humidity, bearings, conditions, datetimes and every other field are as in the metric file. The metric file's notes follow; their numbers are metric. State is the core snapshot. Forecasts were built from source (weather.py and the weatherflow4py library's ha_forecast) run over the test fixture forecast.json. The test does not freeze the clock; now is the first hourly entry's time (the fixture's current conditions are from 2023-12-28T17:51:58Z). Nothing filters past entries: the integration returns every entry the API sends (the fixture has 10 days and 229 hours). Datetimes end in 'Z', not '+00:00'. Daily datetime is the station's local midnight given in UTC (07:00Z here, for a UTC-7 station). Daily sets is_daytime, cloud_coverage, uv_index and wind_bearing to null on every entry and carries only condition, temperature, templow and precipitation_probability as values. Hourly wind_gust_speed is truncated to whole m/s before conversion, so it moves in steps of 3.6 km/h. The state's pressure is station pressure (795.8 hPa at altitude), while hourly pressure is sea-level pressure (about 1020 hPa). The state has no apparent_temperature although the API sends feels_like. Unknown icons become 'exceptional'; hourly condition is null when the API sends no icon; hourly apparent_temperature, pressure, uv_index and precipitation_probability are optional in the library. No changes were needed for realism: current readings and the forecast are the station's own recorded data from minutes apart, so the differences between them (27 % vs 50 % humidity, 7.2 vs 28.8 km/h wind) are real.",
